    "updated_at": "2025-12-12T21:59:32Z",
    "body": "The problem is that *virtually every `<a>` will trigger this error*, if it contains any query parameters. It's uncommon for people to escape the `&` separating params.\r\n\r\nYes, it's confusing that in `<a href=\"foo?bar&copy=bar\">foo?bar&copy=bar</a>` the attribute works correctly but the text shows a copyright symbol, but forcing checkers to flag all such links as invalid would be a huge issue, I think.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
